# Pool members (Kamailio dispatcher module format).
# format: setid destination flags priority attrs
# flags 8 = probing destination (OPTIONS keepalive)
#
# set 1 -> pool "dids" (least-calls: algorithm 10, needs duid)
1 sip:127.0.0.1:5071 8 10 duid=pbx-a
1 sip:127.0.0.1:5072 8 10 duid=pbx-b

# set 2 -> pool "lab-failover" (deterministic serial order: algorithm 8).
# This pool exists only to make the wire-test traces reproducible; priority
# higher priority first makes pbx-a the first attempt and pbx-b the failover.
2 sip:127.0.0.1:5071 8 10 duid=pbx-a
2 sip:127.0.0.1:5072 8 5 duid=pbx-b

# Real members are added per deployment, e.g. (RFC 5737 documentation addresses):
# 1 sip:192.0.2.10:5060 8 10 duid=pbx-1
# 1 sip:192.0.2.11:5060 8 10 duid=pbx-2
